WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.455
What is left: a white dwarf.

00:03.155 --> 00:10.903
Sirius, the brightest star in the night sky, has a companion we do not draw: it is ten thousand times fainter.

00:11.353 --> 00:14.416
It is a white dwarf, the core of a dead star.

00:14.866 --> 00:20.637
It holds nearly the mass of the Sun in a ball about the size of the Earth, slowly cooling.
